  "tier": "told-once",
  "plain": "Beneath the Giza Plateau in Egypt, where the great pyramids stand, there is said to be \"something like a network of underground tunnels.\" The scientist Filippo Biondi, who scanned the ground there with radar in 2025 alongside his colleague Armando Mei, says the scans came back as \"a mess\" of echoes from underground. He tells it as his own finding, which would mean there are large hidden structures under the pyramids."
